WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:15.831
and Flo were wiping tables.

2
00:00:17.012 --> 00:00:18.592
Flo suddenly looked at her phone.

3
00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.614
"Do you mind if I leave now?"

4
00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:24.395
"Sure," Ally said.

5
00:00:24.415 --> 00:00:25.956
"Is everything all right?"

6
00:00:25.976 --> 00:00:27.917
"Yep! Thanks!"

7
00:00:29.538 --> 00:00:31.019
Flo hurried out of the diner.

8
00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:36.286
"Boy, everything doesn't seem all right with her," Ally thought.

9
00:00:36.306 --> 00:00:38.508
"Something must be wrong.

10
00:00:39.028 --> 00:00:40.669
I'll ask her next time I see her."

11
00:00:43.231 --> 00:00:45.493
Jerry and Sally came in a few minutes later.

12
00:00:46.774 --> 00:00:48.275
Ally greeted them with a smile.

13
00:00:48.295 --> 00:00:51.257
"Are you here to film us again?"

14
00:00:51.277 --> 00:00:53.598
"No," Jerry said.

15
00:00:53.618 --> 00:00:55.580
"We thought we'd grab a bite to eat."

16
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.742
"Well, you're in for a treat."

17
00:00:59.282 --> 00:00:59.883
Ally grinned.

18
00:00:59.903 --> 00:01:04.622
"I don't want to brag, but we're the best restaurant in town!"

19
00:01:06.343 --> 00:01:09.485
Jerry and Sally sat down, and Ally brought them menus.

20
00:01:10.686 --> 00:01:14.369
"This is going to be a fun episode of the show," Jerry said.

21
00:01:14.389 --> 00:01:17.691
"There are good teams in Sandville.

22
00:01:18.531 --> 00:01:20.753
But I think Pepe's is the one to beat."

23
00:01:20.773 --> 00:01:23.135
"Ugh!" Ally thought.

24
00:01:23.155 --> 00:01:25.296
"Well, we're not worried!"

25
00:01:25.656 --> 00:01:26.437
she said brightly.

26
00:01:26.457 --> 00:01:30.500
"Rolling Ray's is going to roll over all the competition!"

27
00:01:32.512 --> 00:01:33.613
"They sure are!"

28
00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:34.654
someone said.

29
00:01:35.454 --> 00:01:36.375
Ally spun around.

30
00:01:36.815 --> 00:01:40.338
Mateo's mother had just entered, followed by Kate and Bethany.

31
00:01:42.419 --> 00:01:43.780
"Dawn, you're here!"

32
00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:45.461
Ally gave Dawn a hug.

33
00:01:45.481 --> 00:01:48.583
"It's good to see you, Ally," Dawn said.

34
00:01:48.603 --> 00:01:51.425
"I ran into the girls on my way over here.

35
00:01:52.186 --> 00:01:53.627
They told me about the cook-off."

36
00:01:53.647 --> 00:01:57.510
"And about our double date," Bethany said.

37
00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.851
"What are you going to wear, Ally?"

38
00:02:00.131 --> 00:02:00.712
Kate asked.

39
00:02:01.736 --> 00:02:04.898
"You should wear something cute but casual," Dawn said.

40
00:02:04.918 --> 00:02:07.220
"I have an idea!

41
00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:11.003
Why don't we all go shopping to find you a new outfit?"

42
00:02:11.023 --> 00:02:15.566
"Sure, that sounds fun," Ally said.

43
00:02:15.586 --> 00:02:17.307
"I finish working soon."

44
00:02:17.327 --> 00:02:20.970
"We'll get something to eat and wait for you," Dawn said.

45
00:02:22.371 --> 00:02:24.492
They sat down, and Kate pulled out her phone.

46
00:02:26.174 --> 00:02:26.914
"Hey, look."

47
00:02:27.875 --> 00:02:29.276
She showed everyone her screen.

48
00:02:30.084 --> 00:02:34.387
"Some of the other food trucks have begun announcing the dishes they'll be serving at the cook-off."

49
00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.509
"Yum!" Bethany said.

50
00:02:37.529 --> 00:02:44.513
"Ella's Eats is going to serve a club sandwich with turkey, chips, a fried egg, and a spicy

51
00:02:44.593 --> 00:02:47.275
sauce." "Spicy eggs?"

52
00:02:47.735 --> 00:02:48.236
Ally said.

53
00:02:48.256 --> 00:02:50.077
"With turkey and chips?

54
00:02:50.997 --> 00:02:51.998
Oh no!

55
00:02:52.658 --> 00:02:54.760
That sounds like Barry's new sandwich.

56
00:02:57.288 --> 00:03:00.691
He's going to have to come up with something else for our team."

57
00:03:00.711 --> 00:03:03.814
"Ally?" Jerry waved her over.

58
00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:05.575
"Bad news.

59
00:03:06.016 --> 00:03:07.757
We just got a text and have to go.

60
00:03:08.938 --> 00:03:10.500
We'll take a rain check on eating here."

61
00:03:12.301 --> 00:03:14.363
Ally scratched her head as they hurried out.

62
00:03:15.384 --> 00:03:17.806
"What does the rain have to do with anything?"

63
00:03:18.126 --> 00:03:18.566
she thought.

64
00:03:20.508 --> 00:03:24.752
Later, after shopping with Dawn and her friends, Ally held up her new outfit.

65
00:03:28.008 --> 00:03:29.208
"What do you think, Alpha?"

66
00:03:29.589 --> 00:03:30.129
Ally asked.

67
00:03:30.149 --> 00:03:33.930
"I think a great many things," Alpha said.

68
00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:36.711
"I think we still have no way to get home.

69
00:03:37.391 --> 00:03:40.192
And I think She snorted.

70
00:03:40.212 --> 00:03:43.412
"Going on a date with a human is dangerous!"

71
00:03:44.393 --> 00:03:45.453
Ally rolled her eyes.

72
00:03:45.473 --> 00:03:48.134
"I meant about my outfit.

73
00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:53.835
And you don't have to remind me all the time that we don't have a way home—yet.

74
00:03:54.676 --> 00:03:57.957
But don't worry, we'll get back to Astralia one day."

75
00:03:57.977 --> 00:04:01.780
"One day on Earth is approximately 24 hours long.

76
00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:07.423
One year on Earth is—" "You don't have to tell me how time works here on Earth either,"

77
00:04:07.883 --> 00:04:08.383
Ally said.

78
00:04:08.403 --> 00:04:12.086
"But why do you think going on a date is dangerous?

79
00:04:12.586 --> 00:04:14.307
Julius is very nice."

80
00:04:14.327 --> 00:04:20.570
"An Astralian's prime directive is to resolve conflicts and bring peace to the universe," Alpha said.

81
00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:23.052
"Not go on dates with Earthlings.

82
00:04:23.776 --> 00:04:27.957
You are getting distracted, Allyzooba, and becoming more and more like a human."

83
00:04:27.977 --> 00:04:31.338
"That's not true," Ally snapped.

84
00:04:31.358 --> 00:04:32.558
"And I'll prove it.

85
00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:34.719
Humans can't throw their voices.”

86
00:04:35.799 --> 00:04:36.920
Ally looked out the window.

87
00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:39.940
There was a man walking a dog past the house.

88
00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.741
"Cute dog!"

89
00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:44.042
Ally said, throwing her voice behind them.

90
00:04:44.062 --> 00:04:46.482
"Huh?" The man looked confused.

91
00:04:46.502 --> 00:04:48.763
"Rover, did you hear that?"

92
00:04:48.783 --> 00:04:52.744
"See?" Ally said gleefully.

93
00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:54.961
"I'm nothing like a human!

94
00:04:55.642 --> 00:04:58.184
Plus, I'm being very helpful on this planet.

95
00:04:58.644 --> 00:05:02.688
I'm helping Barry with the contest so he can take special cooking classes.

96
00:05:03.208 --> 00:05:05.610
I'm helping Mateo buy a rare comic book."

97
00:05:08.052 --> 00:05:10.874
"Those are acceptable missions," Alpha mumbled.

98
00:05:11.275 --> 00:05:12.916
But she didn't sound very impressed.

99
00:05:12.936 --> 00:05:15.578
"Thank you," Ally said.

100
00:05:15.598 --> 00:05:21.143
"Just don't forget that I'm allowed to have some fun on Earth while I'm helping humans and bringing

101
00:05:21.203 --> 00:05:22.344
peace to the universe."

102
00:05:23.436 --> 00:05:26.400
"Fun?" Alpha snorted again.

103
00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:28.402
"Fun does not compute."

104
00:05:29.623 --> 00:05:33.588
"Well, I hope it does for my date with Julius," Ally said.

105
00:05:33.608 --> 00:05:37.472
"Because I really like him, and I hope he likes me too!"

106
00:05:40.796 --> 00:05:44.560
With that, Ally turned Alpha off and put away her new outfit.
